# Polyglot Multi-Target ETL Pipeline (SQLite & MongoDB)

## 📌 Overview
An enterprise-grade hybrid ETL pipeline engineered to ingest messy retail transactions (CSV) alongside semi-structured customer feedback logs (JSON). The pipeline performs data deduplication, missing value imputation, and ISO date standardization before storing transformed data into a dual-target architecture: a relational SQLite database (star schema) and a Document NoSQL MongoDB database.

## 🛠 Tech Stack
* **Language:** Python 3.x, SQL
* **Data Transformation:** pandas, NumPy, JSON parsing
* **Relational Storage:** SQLite (`retail_warehouse.db`)
* **NoSQL Storage:** MongoDB (`pymongo`)
* **Architecture:** Polyglot Persistence / Multi-Target Ingestion

## ⚡ Core Pipeline Architecture

```text
               ┌───────────────────────────┐
               │ warehouse_messy_data.csv  │
               └─────────────┬─────────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
 ┌────────────────┐   ┌─────────────┐   ┌───────────────────────────┐
 │ feedback.json  ├──►│ Python ETL  ├──►│ SQLite (Relational OLAP)  │
 └────────────────┘   └──────┬──────┘   └───────────────────────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                      ┌─────────────┐
                      │ MongoDB     │
                      │ (Document)  │
                      └─────────────┘
Extraction: Ingests transaction records (warehouse_messy_data.csv) and generates/parses customer feedback and device info payloads from landing_zone/raw_feedback_logs.json.

Transformation & Data Cleansing:

Removes duplicate transactions.

Standardizes date formats to ISO-8601 (YYYY-MM-DD).

Imputes missing customer_id flags and numerical column anomalies.

Reshapes and merges nested JSON metadata (customer ratings, reviews, IP/device logs) onto core sales records using transaction lookup keys.

Dual-Target Loading:

Relational Target: Normalizes data into fact_sales and dim_store tables inside SQLite.

Document Target: Inserts rich nested JSON documents into MongoDB collection (sales_documents).